"""Bottom screen dashboard (AYN Thor, AYANEO Pocket DS, or any second panel).

Runs inside the bottom-screen gamescope (bottom-screen-session), which drives
the second panel through a DRM lease from the Game Mode gamescope. This file is
the backend: a small HTTP API on 127.0.0.1 for the QML UI (qml/Main.qml), which
it starts and restarts.

  Steam buttons   press Quick Access / Steam / keyboard / screenshot on the
                  virtual Deck pad (InputPlumber SendButtonChord), so Steam's
                  menus open on the main screen
  controls        performance profile + fan boost (konkrd request socket),
                  brightness (thor-backlightd on the Thor, logind elsewhere),
                  volume (wpctl), stick lights (konkrd)
  stats           frame rate, CPU/GPU load and clocks, temperatures, power,
                  memory, fan, battery and time left
  apps            any desktop app, pinned or from the list, runs full screen
                  on the bottom panel; a swipe up from the bottom edge (or the
                  app switcher) comes back here. Text fields in them open the
                  bottom screen's own keyboard (qml/Keyboard.qml)
  top screen      the Trackpad and Keyboard pages move a virtual mouse and
                  keyboard that only the top screen sees

Settings: ~/.config/steamos-arm/bottom-screen.json
"""
